===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*meh₁-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|mone}}, from {{inh|en|ang|mōna||moon}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*mānō}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*mēnô||moon}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*mḗh₁n̥s||moon, month}}, probably from {{m|ine-pro|*meh₁-||to measure}}.
{{col-top|2|cognates and doublets}}
Cognate with {{cog|sco|mone}}, {{m|sco|mune}}, {{m|sco|muin|t=moon}}, {{cog|frr|muun|t=moon}}, {{cog|stq|Moune|t=moon}}, {{cog|fy|moanne|t=moon}}, {{cog|nl|maan|t=moon}}, {{cog|de|Mond|t=moon}}, {{cog|da|måne|t=moon}}, {{cog|nb|måne|t=moon}}, {{cog|nn|måne|t=moon}}, {{cog|sv|måne|t=moon}}, {{cog|fo|máni|t=moon}}, {{cog|is|máni|t=moon}}, {{cog|la|mēnsis|t=month}}. See also {{m|en|month}}, a related term within Indo-European.
{{col-bottom}}

