===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive|colloquial}} To display one's [[buttock]]s to, typically as a [[jest]], [[insult]], or [[protest]].
#: {{cot|en|flash|streak}}
#: {{ux|en|The hooligans '''mooned''' the riot police.}}
#: {{ux|en|It was ill-advised of Sam to '''moon''' the photographer during the shoot.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|colloquial}} To [[gaze]] at [[lovingly]] or in [[adoration]].
#* {{RQ:Lindsay Age of Consent|year=1962|page=164|passage=Bradly stood bewitched, '''mooning''' at the moon. Betimes he bent in a grotesque posture and looked at it between his legs, which was to rid his mind of preconceived colour values by seeing them upside down.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|colloquial}} (''usually followed by'' '''over''' ''or'' '''after''') To [[fuss]] over something [[adoringly]]; to be [[infatuate]]d with someone.
#: {{ux|en|Sarah '''mooned''' over Sam's photograph for months.}}
#: {{ux|en|You've been '''mooning''' after her forever; why not just ask her out?}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=January 12, 2017|author=Jesse Hassenger| title=A literal monster truck is far from the stupidest thing about Monster Trucks| work=The Onion AV Club| url=http://www.avclub.com/review/literal-monster-truck-far-stupidest-thing-about-mo-248111| passage=On some level, the filmmakers behind Monster Trucks must have recognized the ill fit of Till playing a teenager, because they cast Jane Levy, a 27-year-old who can pass for younger but not a decade younger, as Meredith, a nerdy classmate of Tripp’s who '''moons''' over him as she insists on making an appointment to tutor him in biology.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|author=HarryBlank|work=w:SCP Foundation|title=Working Wonders|date=24 September 2023|url=https://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/26-working-wonders|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20240525140823/https://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/26-working-wonders|archivedate=25 May 2024|accessdate=25 May 2024|text="No, you're right." Udo shook this newest distraction out of her head. She knew it would come creeping back in through the ears in due time, just as she knew the best way to dispel it was to finish the job and link up with the rest of the Site. In any event, there was something in what Brenda had said that didn't make sense... "But why would he be '''mooning''' over her, if she's still awake?"</p><p>"Because he's with V—"</p><p>"Veiksaar!" Udo fairly shouted, slapping her forehead. "Oh, shit. This is going to take a lot of getting used to."}}
# To [[spend time]] [[idly]], [[absent-mindedly]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1898|author=Joseph Conrad|title=[[s:Youth (Conrad)|Youth]]|passage=We were only three on board. The poor old skipper '''mooned''' in the cabin.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2001|author=Stephen King|title=w:[[The Death of Jack Hamilton]]|passage=I '''mooned''' around. I was mighty sick of the room by then.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To expose to the rays of the Moon.
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[adorn]] with moons or [[crescent]]s.
# {{lb|en|cryptocurrency|of a coin or token}} To [[rise]] in price rapidly or suddenly.
#: {{ux|en|It is impractical if a currency '''moons''' and plummets often.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Mark Grabowski|title=Cryptocurrencies: A Primer on Digital Money|year=2019|publisher=Routledge|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=0KeaDwAAQBAJ&pg=PT74&dq=%22mooned%22+bitcoin&hl=&cd=5&source=gbs_api#v=onepage&q=%22mooned%22%20bitcoin&f=false|isbn=978-0-429-51357-2|passage=I've followed several of the most popular crypto pundits on Twitter and discovered they constantly brag about their one big Hail Mary pick that '''mooned''' but neglect to mention – or delete – their numerous fumbles.}}
# {{lb|en|card games}} To [[shoot the moon]].

